<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Decimus Junius Brutus Callaicus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2nd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Decimus Junius Brutus Callaicus was a Roman general and consul in 138 BCE. Governing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania-ulterior">Hispania Ulterior</a>, he campaigned against the Lusitanians after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viriathus">Viriathus</a> and in 137 BCE marched north across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douro">Douro</a> and Minho against the Callaeci, earning the surname Callaicus. He also settled Valentia, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, in 138 BCE.</p></div>
